! SEED=1
! GAME=../entharion/glulx-checkers/windowtest-r2-s110119.ulx

# Andrew Plotkin's window explorer: it opens, arranges, and closes a
# second window on command and reports what the library did with each
# one. On a stream of text a second window is kept but not shown, so
# what this recording proves is the library's side, which is what the
# checker is asking about.

windows
size
styles
streams

# [glk #link_events] The links. The game prints two of them and asks
# to hear when one is selected; the script touches one by its value.
# The game answers with the value, the window it came from, and the
# state of the line it was typing, which it cancels and asks for
# again, so this also shows a link arriving while a line is pending.
link
<link 1>
<link 2>

# A second window above the first, three rows of a text grid, then the
# same questions again: the tree now has a pair window with the two of
# them under it, and the sizes are the split the library worked out.
open top grid 3
windows
size

# The game asks about links in the new window too, and gives it links
# 3 and 4 of its own. A console has no pointer to aim, so the display
# hands a link to the first window waiting for one, which is now the
# text grid: the game says so, and says its own links are there.
link
<link 3>

poll
close
windows

quit
